From 3b4a4c322c344210d1a6ad9d76d07a80cbc6c19e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 01:06:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add the Dates.care brand mark and wire up the site icons

The site shipped with no icons at all: no favicon, no apple-touch-icon,
no manifest. Every browser tab showed the blank-page glyph, an installed
shortcut had nothing to display, and the Organization schema pointed at
https://dates.care/logo.png, which does not exist.

The mark is two rings meeting side by side - two people, joined - with a
D in one and a C in the other, and the heart sitting across the join
holding them together. The heart is itself two halves, seam through the
notch between the lobes, one lobe each: the same idea told twice at two
scales. It reads D-heart-C.

Two artworks ship, not one. The full mark needs room: below about 32px
the ring overlap closes up and the letters disappear. So the favicon
drops to the heart alone on the same tile - one brand at two densities,
rather than one artwork that turns to mush in a browser tab.

Letterforms are drawn as geometry rather than type, so the SVG carries
no font dependency and cannot render wrong on a machine that lacks the
face.

Chosen by rendering every candidate at 256/120/64/40/24/16px on light
and dark backgrounds and looking, not by judging them at full size:
dark letters merged into the dark rings and went muddy, and concentric
rings read as a halo rather than as two people.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GPipWR1y6Y6pKtE8MNzisU
